{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1473428844,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxNzYwMTM4MTM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/783","origin":"github"},"title":"Scope limit for meta data functionality? ","message":"I am currently working on this:\n\nhttps://github.com/INCF/BIDS2ISATab\n\nThere are several aspect regarding the purpose of this tool  that could be done more comprehensively in a datalad-context. The goal is to generate an ISATab meta data set from a BIDS dataset that is considered valid and complete for submission to ScientificData.\n\nOne present limitation is the assumption that each assay/file lives in a single dataset on a single sever. We could do better than that in a fully automated way.\n\nQuestion is: do we consider this \"in scope\"?\n\nIt would need some kind of meta data export script, that queries datalad for some information about the content (mostly availabilty), but is otherwise rather specific giving a certain native meta data type.","files":null}]}